/**
 * @page topic_tui Terminal UI (TUI)
 * @ingroup module_ui
 * @brief The interactive terminal screens used by client, server, and tools.
 *
 * @section tui_runtime Runtime model
 *
 * The TUI is a snapshot-driven presentation layer. Session, server, media,
 * discovery, and diagnostic workers publish state; `lib/tui/controller.c`
 * chooses and renders the active screen. No producer should call `printf()` or
 * write ANSI sequences directly while a live screen owns the terminal.
 *
 * @section tui_modes Main screens
 *
 * - Media: live ASCII video, audio visualizations, FPS, and playback controls.
 * - Splash/status: startup, connection, discovery, and server state.
 * - Help: generated from the same shortcut definitions used by dispatch.
 * - Logs: level-filtered output with interactive search.
 * - Statistics: runtime counters and rates.
 * - Sync diagnostics: debug-only lock, condition, and atomic activity.
 * - Prompts, notices, mDNS selection, update, and error screens: modal overlays.
 *
 * @section tui_controls Controls
 *
 * Press `?` from an interactive screen for context-sensitive help. The complete
 * shortcut reference, including build-dependent controls, is in
 * @ref topic_keyboard_shortcuts. Prompts use the shared UTF-8 line editor;
 * Escape cancels and Enter accepts unless a screen documents a different action.
 *
 * @section tui_resize Resize and output
 *
 * Screens calculate their own minimum dimensions. A resize can occur without a
 * new media frame, so the controller checks geometry on its presentation tick.
 * Paused media retains its last frame and clips it after a smaller resize rather
 * than resuming capture. Redirected and non-TTY output renders synchronously.
 *
 * @section tui_debug Diagnostics
 *
 * Debug builds can expose sync and errno-stack inspectors. These are sampled
 * diagnostic views, not atomic snapshots of every application lock. Use
 * `--sync-state`, `--log-file`, and `--grep` when investigating a hang; keep
 * symbolization and logging out of realtime media loops.
 *
 * @section tui_testing Testing
 *
 * The PTY integration suite exercises startup-small, resize recovery, covered
 * input, help restoration, prompts, recording, redirected snapshots, and
 * shutdown:
 * @code{.sh}
 * uv run --project tests/ascii_chat_tests --frozen python -m pytest \
 *   tests/python/integration/terminal_ui --ascii-chat-binary build/bin/ascii-chat
 * @endcode
 *
 * @see topic_ui
 * @see topic_keyboard_shortcuts
 * @see md_docs_2session-tui.html
 * @see md_docs_2terminal-ui.html
 */
